Since $f$ is an isomorphism:

\begin{align*}
	\funimage{f}{A_a} &= \funimage{f}{\Setabs{x \in A}{x < a}}\\
	&= \funimage{f}{\Setabs{f^{-1}(y) \in A}{f^{-1}(y) < a}} \\
	&= \Setabs{y \in B}{y \lessdot f(a)} \\
	&=B_{f(a)} 
\end{align*}
And $\funrestrictionto{f}{A_a}$ preserves order because $f$ does.
